- Story & Context: Recorded beside an open pit stove at the Pozo Hondo waystation while boiling sheep head broth, the session sparked when Mateo accidentally dropped a sputtering solar cable into a tray of fried alliums, causing the salvaged Roland vocoder to emit a howling metallic drone that Ximena immediately matched with an unhinged, circular-breathed sax skronk over a furious 95-BPM dembow beat. As the circuit hissed with scented fat, Mateo spat rapid-fire couplets across the frying pan, howling the hook, "Muerde el cobre si tienes hambre y traga la chispa pura." The track ends with the unedited crash of an aluminum pot tipping into the coals just as the drum machine runs out of voltage.
